<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 250–231 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Agron of Illyria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agron was king of the Ardiaean kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyria">Illyria</a> from about 250 to 231 BCE. He built up a strong fleet and army and extended his power along the eastern Adriatic coast, and in 231 BCE, as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, his forces defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aetolians">Aetolians</a> at Medion. After his sudden death his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teuta">Teuta</a> ruled as regent for his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pinnes">Pinnes</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agron.jpg" alt="Agron" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ballist illlyrian · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ardiaei_Dynasty.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
